# SMARTWAVE PMS — F&B BILLING, ROOM CHARGES, GUEST FOLIO, FRONT DESK SETTLEMENT, RECEIPTS, AND TAX CONFIGURATION

## PROJECT CONTEXT

We are updating the existing SmartWave PMS, a commercial hotel Property Management System built with Firebase, Firestore, and the existing application architecture.

The objective is to improve and properly integrate the Food & Beverage (F&B) module with the Front Desk, Guest Account, Folio, Payment, Receipt, Tax Configuration, and Financial Reporting modules.

This is an enhancement to the existing PMS, NOT a new system.

## CRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS

1. Do not rewrite, replace, restructure, or scatter existing business logic.
2. Do not create a separate financial calculation engine for F&B.
3. Do not duplicate existing payment, folio, tax, receipt, or guest-account logic.
4. First inspect the existing F&B module and its connections to the Front Desk, guest accounts, payment records, tax configuration, and financial reports.
5. Reuse the existing shared financial engine, transaction services, Firestore collections, calculation functions, and existing data structures wherever possible.
6. Do not introduce unnecessary new collections, duplicate fields, or parallel financial workflows.
7. Do not modify unrelated PMS modules.
8. Do not change existing room reservation, room pricing, checkout, housekeeping, guest registration, corporate billing, or other business logic unless a specific integration adjustment is strictly necessary.
9. Preserve all existing working functionality, permissions, configurations, and financial records.
10. Do not overwrite existing Firestore security rules. Append or modify only the necessary rules while preserving existing access controls.
11. Do not introduce Firestore indexes.
12. Maintain the existing user interface design system and navigation structure.
13. All changes must be compatible with existing Firestore data and existing hotel operations.
14. Implement the necessary changes directly within the existing modules rather than scattering functionality throughout the PMS.
15. Before making changes, identify the existing source of truth for each financial operation and reuse it.

