# MODULE 1: F&B BILLING WORKFLOW

The F&B module must support restaurant, bar, lounge, room service, and other configured hotel food and beverage outlets.

Each outlet should have its own operational identity while using the hotel's shared financial system.

The system must support:

- Dine-in orders.
- Room service.
- Takeaway orders.
- Restaurant and bar orders.
- Table management.
- Menu items and categories.
- Configurable menu prices.
- Item quantities.
- Modifiers and add-ons.
- Kitchen order tickets.
- Order status.
- Discounts and promotional codes where permitted.
- Tax calculation.
- Service charge where applicable.
- Direct payment.
- Charge to room.
- Split payment.
- Partial payment.
- Refunds.
- Transaction cancellation and correction.
- F&B sales reporting.

Every transaction must have a unique reference number and retain its relationship to the outlet, cashier, guest, payment, and corresponding PMS financial records.

## F&B BILLING PRINCIPLE

The F&B module must distinguish between:

1. An order that has been created.
2. An order that has been prepared or served.
3. A bill that has been finalised.
4. A bill that has been paid.
5. A bill that has been posted to a guest folio.
6. A bill that has been partially settled.
7. A bill that has been refunded or corrected.

Serving food must not automatically mean that the bill has been paid.

Closing an order must not automatically mean that the hotel has received money.

