# MODULE 5: FRONT DESK CHECKOUT AND SETTLEMENT

When a guest charged F&B to their room, the Front Desk must settle the combined outstanding account.

The checkout screen should display the consolidated guest folio.

Example:

Accommodation: ₦180,000

Restaurant: ₦25,000

Bar: ₦10,000

Laundry: ₦5,000

Total charges: ₦220,000

Payments received before checkout: ₦180,000

Outstanding balance: ₦40,000

The Front Desk should be able to see exactly which transactions make up the ₦40,000.

The cashier should not need to open the F&B module to understand the outstanding bill.

## CHECKOUT PAYMENT WORKFLOW

1. Open the guest's account.
2. Display all charges and previously recorded payments.
3. Display the outstanding balance.
4. Allow the guest to settle the balance using supported payment methods.
5. Record the actual payment.
6. Update the folio balance.
7. Update the payment status.
8. Generate the appropriate receipt and invoice.
9. Complete checkout only according to the existing PMS checkout rules.

Do not automatically settle outstanding F&B charges simply because checkout has been initiated.

Do not allow a guest to check out with an unpaid balance if existing hotel policy blocks owing balances.

If the existing PMS supports corporate billing or authorised outstanding balances, preserve that functionality and route eligible charges through the existing corporate billing logic.

