# MODULE 8: F&B TAX CONFIGURATION

The F&B module must use the existing PMS tax configuration and shared financial calculation engine.

Do not create independent tax calculations within the restaurant, bar, Front Desk, or receipt modules.

## TAX CONFIGURATION REQUIREMENTS

The Hotel Admin must be able to configure:

- Tax name.
- Tax percentage.
- Tax type.
- Tax jurisdiction.
- Tax applicability.
- Tax-inclusive pricing.
- Tax-exclusive pricing.
- Taxable menu items.
- Tax-exempt menu items.
- Multiple applicable taxes where legally permitted.
- Tax calculation order.
- Whether service charge is taxable.
- Whether discounts reduce the taxable base.
- Effective date.
- Tax activation and deactivation.
- Tax reporting category.

Examples of tax types:

- VAT.
- Applicable state or local consumption taxes.
- Other legally applicable configured taxes.

These are configurable examples, not automatic tax assignments.

## TAX RULES

1. Do not hardcode tax percentages into F&B menu items or calculation functions.
2. Tax must be retrieved from the shared tax configuration.
3. Each menu item should inherit its applicable tax classification.
4. Tax must be calculated consistently at the outlet and Front Desk.
5. The tax breakdown must remain traceable.
6. Discounts must be applied according to the configured taxable-base rules.
7. Tax-inclusive prices must not have tax added twice.
8. Tax-exclusive prices must calculate the applicable tax correctly.
9. Tax exemptions must be applied only when properly configured and authorised.
10. Tax changes must not silently recalculate previously completed transactions.
11. Historical transactions must preserve the tax configuration and rates applied when they were originally posted.
12. Tax adjustments must be auditable.
13. Refunds and cancellations must reverse the appropriate tax components.
14. Do not allow staff to manually change tax amounts without the appropriate permissions and audit trail.

---

# MODULE 9: TAX-INCLUSIVE AND TAX-EXCLUSIVE PRICING

The system must support both pricing models.

## TAX-EXCLUSIVE EXAMPLE

Assume:

Menu item price before tax: ₦10,000

Configured VAT: 7.5%

VAT: ₦750

Total: ₦10,750

The customer pays ₦10,750.

The system must display:

Subtotal: ₦10,000

VAT: ₦750

Total: ₦10,750

## TAX-INCLUSIVE EXAMPLE

Assume:

Displayed menu price: ₦10,750

Configured VAT: 7.5%

The VAT component is included in the displayed price.

Taxable amount before VAT: ₦10,000

VAT component: ₦750

Total payable: ₦10,750

The system must not add another ₦750 to the existing ₦10,750.

## TAX CALCULATION VALIDATION

Use the shared calculation engine to verify the actual taxable base and tax amount.

Do not independently calculate tax in the receipt, guest folio, and checkout screens.

All three screens must display the same tax breakdown derived from the same financial transaction.

---

# MODULE 10: SERVICE CHARGE CONFIGURATION

Service charges must be configurable independently of tax.

The Hotel Admin should be able to configure:

- Service charge percentage.
- Service charge applicability.
- Outlets where it applies.
- Menu items where it applies.
- Whether it is included in displayed prices.
- Whether it is taxable under the configured jurisdiction.
- Effective date.
- Applicable exemptions.

The system must not automatically assume that every F&B transaction attracts a service charge.

The system must calculate service charge according to the configured hotel policy.

Do not allow the same service charge to be applied at the F&B outlet and then again at Front Desk checkout.

A charge posted to the guest folio must retain its original service charge and tax breakdown.

