# MODULE 11: DISCOUNTS, PROMOTIONS, AND COMPLIMENTARY F&B

F&B discounts must integrate with the existing discount and promotional-code system wherever applicable.

The system should support:

- Percentage discounts.
- Fixed-amount discounts.
- Approved promotional codes.
- Staff-authorised discounts.
- Complimentary meals.
- Complimentary drinks.
- Manager-approved adjustments.

Preserve the existing Hotel Admin discount permissions and approval logic.

Do not allow F&B staff to create unrestricted discounts if the existing PMS requires Hotel Admin approval.

## DISCOUNT RULES

- Record the original amount.
- Record the discount amount.
- Record the final taxable amount according to the configured tax rules.
- Record the user who applied the discount.
- Record the approval where required.
- Do not allow discounts to alter already-paid transactions without a correction process.
- Prevent duplicate discount application.
- Preserve existing corporate discount and promotional-code rules.

Complimentary transactions must be recorded as authorised zero-charge or discounted transactions according to the existing accounting design.

They must not be falsely recorded as cash sales.

