# MODULE 12: TRANSACTION CORRECTIONS, REFUNDS, AND VOIDING

The system must preserve financial history.

Do not permanently delete completed financial transactions.

If an F&B transaction is incorrect:

- Use the existing void, reversal, adjustment, or refund functionality.
- Record the reason.
- Record the user who initiated the correction.
- Record the approving user where required.
- Preserve the original transaction.
- Link the correction to the original transaction.
- Reverse the appropriate financial and tax effects.
- Update the guest folio through the shared financial engine.
- Update the relevant reports.

If a room charge has already been posted, correcting the F&B transaction must also correct the guest folio.

Do not reverse the outlet transaction without correcting the corresponding PMS posting.

Do not refund an amount that was never actually received as payment.

A room charge is an outstanding receivable, not cash received.

