# MODULE 13: F&B AND FRONT DESK TRANSACTION RECONCILIATION

Implement the necessary reporting and reconciliation using the existing reporting architecture.

The system should allow authorised users to reconcile:

- Total F&B sales.
- Direct F&B payments.
- F&B room charges.
- Split payments.
- Outstanding room-posted F&B charges.
- F&B refunds.
- F&B discounts.
- Tax collected.
- Service charges.
- Front Desk settlements of F&B charges.

## RECONCILIATION RULE

F&B room charges must be traceable from:

F&B bill → PMS folio posting → Guest account → Front Desk payment → Final invoice.

Each stage must share the appropriate transaction reference.

The system must prevent the same F&B transaction from being posted to the guest folio twice.

The system must also prevent an F&B room charge from being recorded as cash or card revenue received before actual payment.

## REPORTS

Add the necessary F&B reporting capability without duplicating existing reports.

The system should support:

- F&B sales by outlet.
- F&B sales by cashier.
- F&B sales by payment method.
- Room-charge transactions.
- F&B transactions posted to guest folios.
- F&B payments received at the outlet.
- F&B charges settled at Front Desk.
- Outstanding F&B charges.
- F&B refunds.
- F&B tax report.
- Service charge report.
- Daily outlet reconciliation.
- Room-posting reconciliation.
- Transaction correction report.

Reports must use the existing financial records and must not independently recalculate sales or payments.

