# MODULE 15: FIRESTORE AND REAL-TIME INTEGRATION

Inspect the existing Firestore schema before implementing.

Reuse existing collections and references wherever possible.

Do not create duplicate guest folios, payment records, or financial transactions.

Ensure that:

- Room-charge postings appear immediately in the Front Desk guest account.
- Payment updates appear immediately in the relevant account.
- The F&B outlet can identify the transaction status.
- The Front Desk can identify the originating F&B bill.
- The correct guest and stay references are preserved.
- Existing Firestore rules enforce appropriate permissions.
- Updates do not overwrite unrelated fields.
- Existing records remain backward-compatible.
- Real-time listeners are used consistently with the current application architecture.

Use the existing transaction and concurrency controls to prevent duplicate postings, repeated payments, and race conditions.

If a posting fails, do not silently mark the F&B bill as successfully charged to the room.

Provide a clear error state and allow an authorised retry without creating duplicate charges.

