# MODULE 16: ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Before considering the enhancement complete, test the following scenarios.

### Test 1: Restaurant payment

Guest pays the complete bill at the restaurant.

Expected result: Paid F&B transaction, correct outlet report, no duplicate outstanding room charge.

### Test 2: Complete room charge

Guest charges the entire restaurant bill to the room.

Expected result: Correct F&B bill, correct guest folio debit, correct Front Desk outstanding balance, correct receipt.

### Test 3: Partial outlet payment

Guest pays part of the bill and charges the remainder to the room.

Expected result: Actual payment recorded, only the remainder posted to the folio, no duplicate charge.

### Test 4: Split cash and card

Guest pays through two methods.

Expected result: Both payment records are associated with the same bill and the correct total is settled.

### Test 5: Front Desk partial payment

Guest pays only part of the outstanding folio.

Expected result: Payment is recorded, balance remains outstanding, and the account is not falsely marked fully paid.

### Test 6: Tax-inclusive menu price

Expected result: Tax is extracted correctly and not added twice.

### Test 7: Tax-exclusive menu price

Expected result: Tax is added correctly using the existing tax engine.

### Test 8: Room charge disabled

Expected result: F&B staff cannot post a room charge or bypass existing restrictions.

### Test 9: Guest checkout

Expected result: All room-posted F&B charges appear in the consolidated guest account and are settled through the existing checkout process.

### Test 10: Refund

Expected result: Refund and reversal are recorded correctly, with corresponding guest folio and tax adjustments.

### Test 11: Duplicate posting prevention

Expected result: Repeated confirmation or network retry cannot create duplicate F&B charges.

### Test 12: Financial reconciliation

Expected result: Outlet sales, guest folio charges, payments, taxes, and outstanding balances reconcile correctly.

### Test 13: Existing PMS functionality

Expected result: Existing reservations, room charges, guest payments, checkout, corporate billing, and financial reports continue to work without regressions.

